{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":282357,"duration_api_ms":441125,"num_turns":26,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"3e530441-1654-46bd-a56a-8e866836a86b","total_cost_usd":1.72793195,"usage":{"input_tokens":7389,"cache_creation_input_tokens":61580,"cache_read_input_tokens":767178,"output_tokens":8186,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":61580,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":7389,"outputTokens":8186,"cacheReadInputTokens":767178,"cacheCreationInputTokens":61580,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.010059,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000},"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":18001,"outputTokens":25640,"cacheReadInputTokens":3500132,"cacheCreationInputTokens":177327,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7178729500000001,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"summary":"Reviewed the molt/mineral budget implementation across shrimp.rs, biology.rs, presets.rs, molt_mineral_budget.rs tests, and data files. The feature is well-engineered: the mineral modifier correctly composes GH, Ca, and Mg as independent factors; molt frequency varies by life stage via configurable intervals; failed molts accumulate and increase mortality; events surface actionable cause codes (LowMinerals, PoorCondition, etc.); the 1000-hour soft-vs-hard-water integration test exists with proper assertions. Three substantive issues found: (1) gh_min_d=0.0 passes TOML validation but causes division by zero in two locations, (2) CRITICAL_MOLT_GH_RATIO is a const rather than a named parameter per the AC, (3) inconsistent defensive guards on division by gh_min_d.","amendments":[{"body":"In crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs, `gh_min_d` is validated only as non-negative (>= 0.0) at line 549, unlike `ca_min_mg_per_l` and `mg_min_mg_per_l` which are validated as strictly positive (> 0.0) at lines 646-661. Setting `gh_min_d = 0.0` in a TOML file passes validation but causes division-by-zero panics at shrimp.rs:356 (`(params.gh_min_d - gh_d) / params.gh_min_d`) and shrimp.rs:1247 (`gh_d / params.gh_min_d`). Fix: add `gh_min_d` to the strictly-positive validation block alongside `ca_min_mg_per_l` and `mg_min_mg_per_l` (lines 646-661), or add a dedicated check `if self.gh_min_d <= 0.0 { return Err(...) }` near line 562.","rationale":"This is a reachable panic from user-supplied data. The TOML validation is the primary defense and it has a gap specifically for gh_min_d. The inconsistency with ca_min/mg_min suggests this was an oversight rather than intentional."},{"body":"In crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs, `CRITICAL_MOLT_GH_RATIO` (line 12, value 0.3) is a file-level `const` that determines when molts unconditionally fail (GH < 30% of gh_min_d). The acceptance criteria require 'All molt-related thresholds and modifiers are named parameters in species/process data, not hardcoded constants.' Move this to a field on `ShrimpRuntimeParams` (e.g., `critical_molt_gh_ratio: f64` with default 0.3) and add a corresponding optional field in `ShrimpPreset`.","rationale":"This is the only binary molt-failure threshold that is not species-configurable. It directly controls whether molts can ever succeed and is clearly a 'molt-related threshold' per the AC. Different species might tolerate different GH deficit ratios."},{"body":"In crates/tank_core/src/systems/shrimp.rs, line 439 uses `.max(0.01)` as a defensive guard against gh_min_d=0 (`gh_d / params.gh_min_d.max(0.01)`), but lines 356 and 1247 divide by `params.gh_min_d` without any guard. Even after adding TOML validation for gh_min_d > 0, add consistent `.max(f64::EPSILON)` or `.max(0.01)` guards at lines 356 and 1247 to match the defensive pattern already established at line 439.","rationale":"Defense in depth. The existing guard at line 439 shows the author was aware of the risk but didn't apply it consistently. Direct construction of ShrimpRuntimeParams in tests or programmatic use bypasses TOML validation entirely."}]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"7b0a915a-26f9-4072-b656-53d8ab65597b"}
